1
00:04:15,652 --> 00:04:21,652
For some, 13 feels like it was just yesterday. For Jenna, it was.

2
00:08:31,304 --> 00:08:37,304
13 Going on 30 is a comedy, fantasy, romance film directed by Gary Winick.

3
00:12:46,956 --> 00:12:52,956
After total humiliation at her thirteenth birthday party,
Jenna Rink wants to just hide until she's thirty.

4
00:17:02,608 --> 00:17:08,608
Thanks to some magic wishing dust, Jenna's prayer has been answered.

5
00:21:18,260 --> 00:21:24,260
With a knockout body, a fabulous wardrobe, an athlete boyfriend, a dream
job, and superstar friends, this can't be a better life.

6
00:25:33,913 --> 00:25:39,913
But soon Jenna realizes that adult life isn’t as easy as she hoped for.

7
00:29:49,565 --> 00:29:55,565
Jenna Rink, played by Jennifer Garner.

8
00:34:05,217 --> 00:34:11,217
Matt Flamhaff, played by Mark Ruffalo.

9
00:38:20,869 --> 00:38:26,869
Lucy Wyman, played by Judy Greer.

10
00:42:36,521 --> 00:42:42,521
Richard Kneeland, played by Andy Serkis.

11
00:46:52,173 --> 00:46:58,173
Bev Rink, played by Kathy Baker.

12
00:51:07,826 --> 00:51:13,826
Wayne Rink, played by Phil Reeves.

13
00:55:23,478 --> 00:55:29,478
13 Going on 30 (released as Suddenly 30 in some countries) is a 2004 American fantasy romantic comedy film written by Cathy Yuspa and Josh
Goldsmith, directed by Gary Winick, starring Jennifer Garner and Mark Ruffalo, and produced by Susan Arnold and Donna Arkoff Roth.

14
00:59:39,130 --> 00:59:45,130
The film is about a 13-year-old girl in 1987 who awakens to find herself
suddenly 30 years old and living in 2004 as a fashion editor.

15
01:03:54,782 --> 01:04:00,782
13 Going on 30 received generally positive reviews from critics, with many
praising Garner's performance and its nostalgic environment.

16
01:08:10,434 --> 01:08:16,434
It was also praised for its humorous plot and self-empowering message.

17
01:12:26,086 --> 01:12:32,086
The film was also a commercial success, earning $22 million in its first week
and becoming one of the year's biggest-selling DVD rental titles.

18
01:16:41,739 --> 01:16:47,739
Its total box office profit was over $96 million.

19
01:20:57,391 --> 01:21:03,391
Additionally, the soundtrack charted inside the top
50 on the US Billboard 200 chart.

20
01:25:13,043 --> 01:25:19,043
Garner's acting earned her nominations from both the MTV
Movie Awards and the Teen Choice Awards.

21
01:29:28,695 --> 01:29:34,695
The film explores themes of new york city,
photographer, editor-in-chief, time travel, wish.

22
01:33:44,347 --> 01:33:50,347
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
